# Card kinds

A `kind` selects the spec schema a card carries. The envelope is always the same;
the kind changes the payload, not the ontology. The v1 doctrine defines 15 native
kinds plus `External` for forward compatibility.

<Aside title="Three kinds run end-to-end" data-variant="wyrd">

**Data**, **Model**, and **Prompt** are shipped: authored in Python, validated,
saved, and — for Prompt — resolved by the Skald runtime. Every other kind has an
authored spec and JSON Schema but no runtime behind it yet. The tables below mark
each one. See [Cards](/cards/) for per-field reference on the shipped kinds.

</Aside>

